  "stem": "In the \\(xy\\)-plane, the graph of which of the following functions has a \\(y\\)-intercept of \\((0, 7)\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "mcq",
  "choices": {
    "A": "\\(f(x) = 3(7)^{x}\\)",
    "B": "\\(f(x) = 7(3)^{x}\\)",
    "C": "\\(f(x) = (x - 7)^{2}\\)",
    "D": "\\(f(x) = 3^{x} + 4\\)"
  },
  "answer": "B",
  "spr_answers": null,
  "solution": [
    "The \\(y\\)-intercept is the value of \\(f(0)\\).",
    "\\(7(3)^{0} = 7(1) = 7\\), so \\(f(x) = 7(3)^{x}\\) has \\(y\\)-intercept \\((0, 7)\\).",
    "Check the others: \\(3(7)^{0} = 3\\), \\((0 - 7)^{2} = 49\\), \\(3^{0} + 4 = 5\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": {
    "A": "Incorrect. \\(f(0) = 3(7)^{0} = 3\\). In \\(a(b)^{x}\\) the \\(y\\)-intercept is \\(a\\), not \\(b\\).",
    "B": "Correct. \\(f(0) = 7(3)^{0} = 7\\).",
    "C": "Incorrect. \\(f(0) = (-7)^{2} = 49\\). The \\(7\\) here is the \\(x\\)-coordinate of the vertex, \\((7, 0)\\).",
    "D": "Incorrect. \\(f(0) = 3^{0} + 4 = 1 + 4 = 5\\), since \\(3^{0} = 1\\), not \\(3\\)."
  },
  "traps": {
    "A": "concept",
    "C": "concept",
    "D": "arithmetic"
  },
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nrhs = {k: value(v.split('=')[1]) for k, v in choices.items()}\nok = [k for k in rhs if rhs[k].subs(x, 0) == 7]\nassert ok == [answer]",
